Root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect handling of orphan nodes during error conditions in the `ubifs_jnl_update()` and `ubifs_jnl_rename()` functions. Specifically, the code was attempting to delete orphan nodes without verifying if they had been added to the orphan list, leading to potential deletion of non-existent orphan nodes and resulting in error messages indicating missing orphan inodes. The fix involved adding a check to ensure that orphan nodes are only deleted if they were actually added to the orphan list during the operation.
